// ANTI-VENOM AND ANTI-VENOM+ (OSRS, 8 January 2015, "Zulrah - The Solo Snake Boss" - so they are
// ported as OSRS has them, not reinvented). Every field below was read out of a modern OSRS cache
// with tools/models/importosrs.py --dry-run: objs 12905/12907/12909/12911 (anti-venom 4..1) and
// 12913/12915/12917/12919 (anti-venom+ 4..1).
//
// NOTHING WAS IMPORTED, because there was nothing to import. OSRS still draws all eight on the very
// same four vial models this 377 cache already carries - the importer named models 2789, 2697, 2384
// and 2621, which are pack ids 2789=obj_strength4, 2697=obj_guamvial, 2384=obj_2dose1strength and
// 2621=obj_1dose1strength here, the models antidote++ itself uses. A potion is its vial plus one
// recolour, so the only thing that crossed over is the colour: the cache's HSL16 recolour 61->26772
// (anti-venom) and 61->61594 (anti-venom+), converted to the RGB15 a .obj config writes by
// importosrs.hsl16_to_rgb15. That converter was checked on antidote++ first - its 61->11811 comes
// back as 15855->12708, which is exactly what _unpack/377/all.obj already had - and both colours
// were rendered with tools/models/ob2render.py and looked at: anti-venom is a deep green, anti-venom+
// a dark maroon, as OSRS draws them. So this round took no model.pack ids at all.
//
// The 2d icon angles, costs, weights, examines and ops are the cache's own. They are noteable in
// OSRS, hence the cert records. What they DO is in scripts/antivenom.rs2 (making them) and
// player/scripts/consumption/effects/scripts/anti_poison.rs2 (drinking them).

[antivenom4]
name=Anti-venom(4)
desc=4 doses of antivenom potion.
model=obj_strength4
recol1s=15855
recol1d=4293
2dzoom=550
2dxan=84
2dyan=1996
2dyof=-1
weight=35g
cost=440
members=yes
iop1=Drink
iop4=Empty
category=potion
param=cures_poison,yes
param=next_obj_stage,antivenom3
param=decant_potion_enum,potion_antivenom
param=dose_count,4

[cert_antivenom4]
certlink=antivenom4
certtemplate=template_for_cert

